    {
      "id": "justification:l2:lumina-prime:orientation-beacon-v0",
      "node_type": "narrative",
      "subtype": "justification",
      "content": {
        "why": [
          "A civic beacon is useful only when its position claim and delivery are independently provable.",
          "Signed coordinates plus quadrant, sector and ground distance provide a real GPS-like fix rather than a decorative label.",
          "Distance remains spatial data; atom energy remains conserved gating energy.",
          "Built pose precedence preserves the fact that the city was constructed rather than regenerated.",
          "A separately linked emergency authority keeps exceptional public speech explicit, revocable and auditable."
        ],
        "rejected": [
          "using visual distance from the camera because camera projection is not civic location",
          "using embedding distance because semantic proximity is not geometric position",
          "encoding metres as bond energy because energy and spatial measurement are distinct dimensions",
          "always-on emergency capability because it makes every beacon a silent sovereign broadcaster",
          "health inferred from process liveness or glowing animation",
          "a single opaque health score that collapses unrelated failures"
        ]
      }
